      "html": "<ul><li>Scientific name: Hypostomus roseopunctatus Reis, Weber &amp; Malabarba, 1990</li><li>Common name: Rose-spotted Pleco</li><li>IUCN Red List: Least Concern (last assessed 2020)</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1337",
      "html": "<p>South America: La Plata system: Uruguay basin. Recorded from the Uruguay, Miriñay and Upper Uruguay (Pelotas) areas. Type locality: Rio Pelotas at road from Esmeralda to Anita Garibaldi, Rio Grande do Sul, Brazil.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1337",
      "html": "<p>Photographed habitat: Rio Parana, Corrientes State, Argentina.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1337",
      "html": "<p>Breeding: unreported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1337",
      "html": "<p>Etymology: Greek, hypo = under + Greek, stoma = mouth. The specific epithet refers to its rose-coloured (roseus = rose-coloured, red) spots (punctatus = small spots). Other common name: Rosenplettet Sugemalle (Denmark).</p>"
    },
